  <spdx:ListedLicenseException rdf:about="http://spdx.org/licenses/u-boot-exception-2.0">
    <rdfs:seeAlso>http://git.denx.de/?p=u-boot.git;a=blob;f=Licenses/Exceptions</rdfs:seeAlso>
    <spdx:licenseExceptionText>The U-Boot License Exception:

Even though U-Boot in general is covered by the GPL-2.0/GPL-2.0+, this does *not* cover the so-called "standalone" applications that use U-Boot services by means of the jump table provided by U-Boot exactly for this purpose - this is merely considered normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the heading of "derived work".

The header files "include/image.h" and "arch/*/include/asm/u-boot.h" define interfaces to U-Boot. Including these (unmodified) header files in another file is considered normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the heading of "derived work".
-- Wolfgang Denk
</spdx:licenseExceptionText>
    <spdx:exceptionTextHtml>
      &lt;div class="optional-license-text"&gt; 
         &lt;p&gt;&lt;var class="replaceable-license-text"&gt;&lt;span title="can be replaced with the pattern The U-Boot|GPL"&gt; GPL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/var&gt; License Exception:&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;Even though U-Boot in general is covered by the GPL-2.0/GPL-2.0+,
         this does *not* cover the so-called &amp;quot;standalone&amp;quot; applications
         that use U-Boot services by means of the jump table provided
         by U-Boot exactly for this purpose - this is merely considered
         normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the heading of
         &amp;quot;derived work&amp;quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

      &lt;p&gt;The header files &amp;quot;include/image.h&amp;quot; and
         &amp;quot;arch/*/include/asm/u-boot.h&amp;quot; define interfaces to U-Boot.
         Including these (unmodified) header files in another file is
         considered normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the
         heading of &amp;quot;derived work&amp;quot;.
        &lt;br /&gt;
-- Wolfgang Denk
      &lt;/p&gt;

      </spdx:exceptionTextHtml>
    <rdfs:comment>Typically used with GPL-2.0-only or GPL-2.0-or-later</rdfs:comment>
    <spdx:licenseExceptionTemplate>&lt;&lt;beginOptional&gt;&gt;&lt;&lt;var;name="title";original="GPL";match="The U-Boot|GPL"&gt;&gt; License Exception:

&lt;&lt;endOptional&gt;&gt;
Even though U-Boot in general is covered by the GPL-2.0/GPL-2.0+, this does *not* cover the so-called "standalone" applications that use U-Boot services by means of the jump table provided by U-Boot exactly for this purpose - this is merely considered normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the heading of "derived work".

The header files "include/image.h" and "arch/*/include/asm/u-boot.h" define interfaces to U-Boot. Including these (unmodified) header files in another file is considered normal use of U-Boot, and does *not* fall under the heading of "derived work".
-- Wolfgang Denk

</spdx:licenseExceptionTemplate>
